==Strategy==
This stage introduces Sir Rel, a Relic variant of [[Squire Rel]] similar to those encountered in [[Apple Bobbing Ocean]], boasting deceptively powerful stats and strong pushing power. Never underestimate a Sir Rel, for it may be the mistake that causes you to lose a level.

The first Bore here quickly dies to [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], while Nimoy Bore can be stunlocked and killed by [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] and the aforementioned Talented Can Can Cat. The Sir Rel waves are easily countered with strong Area Attackers, such as a good stack of [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]. [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime]] with a meatshield is able to connect onto a Sir Rel horde and deal serious damage to them, with Slime's True Form allowing it to connect onto a Sir Rel without the need of a meatshield. There shouldn't be much of a cash issue due to how quickly the Sir Rels and Bores die, but don't go overboard with spamming your units. Try to clear the stage quickly, because the Sir Rel waves get worse the longer you're in the level.

===3 Crown Strategy===
The Sir Rels are 200%, so running solely brute-force options for the enemies here isn't going to work at all this time around. Instead, try adding [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Master Uril]] to efficiently CC the Sir Rel hordes. The Bores are a lot more tanky since their magnifications are doubled, so you won't have the 1 Crown luxury of being able to kill the first Bore quick. Instead, use the Bore's higher health to your advantage by using them as a stepping stone for units with Wave like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]] to deal with the Sir Rel waves, while you use [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] and Seafarer to Freeze the Bores. If you've got access to the True Forms of UL Mythic Cats, [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]] and [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] are invaluable here. You can also try Research [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder]] to help stall the enemies, but due to the sheer amount of DPS present on the frontline there is a very real chance your Rock can die if unboosted. There's some pretty heavy cash problems early on, which at the worst may force a Rich Cat from your hands, but once you kill the initial Bore you should be good to go.

==Trivia==
*The name "John Gool" is a pun on ''jungle''.
*Prior to [[Version 10.10 Update|Version 10.10]], [[Bore]] was buffed to 300% instead of 200% while [[Nimoy Bore]] was buffed to 800% instead of 600%.

